### Downloaded media (regenerable) — keep out of git history
data/wikidata/**/charts/

### Generated snapshots (regenerable; tracked via the dataset registry, not git)
*.snapshot.json

### OCR-miss staging (regenerable by ChartBlurTool)
data/masks/needs-mask/

### Local run state — follows whatever snapshots this machine happens to have
# The registry the app rewrites on every save; its entries point at snapshots
# that are themselves untracked, so in git it only ever conflicts.
data/wikidata/datasets.json
data/query-log*.txt
data/query-log*.run.json

### Per-run query logs (regenerable; one pair of files per generation run)
# A run writes a .txt transcript and a .run.json beside the domain it generated.
# They are evidence about ONE run on ONE machine, they grow without bound — 132 MB
# of them were pending here — and nothing reads them back. The 25 MB already in
# history stays; this stops the pile growing.
data/wikidata/**/query-log-*.txt
data/wikidata/**/query-log-*.run.json

### Generated correction overlays (rebuilt by the *FixMain tools from a snapshot)
*.autofix.json

### Claude Code
.claude/settings.local.json
